@1000001 = ~I hear your voice... you come into view.~
@1000002 = ~I hear your voice... you come into view.~
@1000003 = ~Aye, there's some books in the guest room for those who are bored and lookin' for something to read. It's got nothin' on the great library, of course, but it's somethin'. They be on the shelf, go ahead and take them, child. They're mostly gatherin' dust these days.~
@1000004 = ~We'd better move quickly, <CHARNAME>. There'll be more of these shapeshifting fiends ahead. Best watch for traps as well—who knows what's been done to this place.~
@1000005 = ~Don't worry, <CHARNAME>. We'll do everything we can to clear out these filth from Candlekeep's walls. You can rest assured of that.~
@1000006 = ~The path to the surface isn't far, <CHARNAME>. You'll be able to find your way out from here.~
@1000007 = ~I'm going to head back now. Someone'll need to report everything that's happened here. Sorry I can't help you more, but I know you'll be fine.~
@1000008 = ~Good luck, <CHARNAME>. Find the bastard who set this up and give him what he deserves... and come back alive.~
@1000009 = ~From Mordaine? To me? Okay, let me have a look...~
@1000010 = ~Oh. Oh... um, well... right, er... thanks for delivering it. I've got to get things ready, quickly...~
@1000011 = ~Aye... don't trust a word from anyone else we find here... I'll put my axe through their skulls first. Fear not, child... we'll see you through this.~
@1000012 = ~Bah! Lies, <CHARNAME>, heed them not. The Watchers never heard anyone speak of such a thing!~
@1000013 = ~By Moradin's hammer! Young Hull, too? This is truly a waking nightmare...~
@1000014 = ~This is as far as we can go, my <PRO_GIRLBOY>. The Watchers must know of what has transpired here... but the end of the path will not be too far ahead.~
@1000015 = ~It pains us that we cannot protect you any further, but you have grown much since you first left. Even though your journey will undoubtedly only become more difficult... I can see you won't need the two of us any longer.~
@1000016 = ~Aye... this is goodbye once more, but I know we will meet again, someday.~
@1000017 = ~Go now, <PRO_GIRLBOY>... go, and live well.~
@1000018 = ~From what I hear, you're also an aspiring arcanist. You almost remind me of myself as a fledging apprentice, such a nostalgic time... I feel as your senior in the practice of the Art, I should do more for you, especially as I hear you will be going on quite the journey.~
@1000019 = ~Though I do not wish to overreach in your development as a mage, I can still give you a head start... here, I have an assortment of spell scrolls that may be useful to you. Pick one, any one. Will it be the scroll of Burning Hands, Friends, Spook, Protection from Evil, or Shield?~
@1000020 = ~Here you are, young one. This is but the beginning—the greater secrets of the Weave are out there. Me, I am far too old to be seeking them. But you have immeasurable potential. Good luck.~
@1000021 = ~Oho, and I see a familiar face taggin' along with you too. Imoen, girl, does my memory fail me, or did I not entrust you with the cleanin' of the rooms upstairs, eh?~
@1000022 = ~Now, haven't I always told you to be honest to your old man? You're spendin' time with <CHARNAME> before <PRO_HESHE> goes, I don't mind it. Just make sure you don't forget before the day's through, aye? You know this old back ain't as good at bendin' over to reach the corners as it used to be.~
@1000023 = ~That's a good girl.~
@1000024 = ~Don't say anything. Just run. I'll be with you soon. You should not see what is to come.~
@1000025 = ~<CHARNAME>, my child...~
@1000026 = ~Perhaps. But I do wonder, however... is this your idea of revenge, boy?~
@1000027 = ~You are a consequence of my past failures. Despite your posturing, you invoke no fear in me, only shame.~
@1000028 = ~You are right that I have failed too many times... but for the last, you are wrong. I have saved that child from becoming a slave to power, as you have. True, <PRO_HISHER> path will be difficult... but <PRO_HESHE> will have hope. Unlike you.~
@1000029 = ~Do what you will, but this will be no victory for you. That child is strong... the day will come when <PRO_HESHE> reaches heights you never shall.~
@1000030 = ~Enough taunts. The debt between us is long overdue... it's high time we settled it at last.~
@1000031 = ~Even in your final moments, you deceive <PRO_HIMHER>. You know full well how this will end.~
@1000032 = ~The past is irrelevant. When I look upon what has become of you and your ward, I consider myself blessed that I was not cursed with such weakness.~
@1000033 = ~But you are well-versed in failure, are you not, old man? You could not save that woman, or the others... and once you are dead, you will not be able to save that whelp.~
@1000034 = ~Indeed? Perhaps I should keep one last breath of life in you instead, so that you will be there to witness the day I properly crush your hope under my heel...~
@1000035 = ~Ah... so you do have a speck of your former fire within you after all. This will be more entertaining than I expected.~
@1000036 = ~Yes, I know. Our time is precious, and our plan is only at its inception. We shall make this quick.~
@1000037 = ~Is that so? Challenge accepted, old man. I shall anticipate the struggle that is to come... a pity you will not be alive to witness it.~
@1000038 = ~Woof!~
@1000039 = ~I see you are here with the... young <CHARNAME>. I take it that means you intend to leave soon, as you've so stubbornly insisted?~
@1000040 = ~Well, I would wish you safe journey, but I doubt that will be the case, given what I know of your intentions. Perhaps you have reconsidered since our last discussion?~
@1000041 = ~Foolish... I have said it before, Gorion. There is a much simpler solution to this inanity. You and I know this to be true.~
@1000042 = ~I would have thought age and comfort would have ridded you of your urge for meddling in affairs that are beyond you. You have chosen peace for all these years, and you will throw it all away for your sentimentality?~
@1000043 = ~Bah! ~
@1000044 = ~Fine. On your own head be it, foolish Harper.~
@1000045 = ~If you are set in your absurd ways, then I shall not expect either of your returns with optimism. But I will repeat my generous advice—you would do best to leave <PRO_HIMHER> in some forgotten ravine and be done with it.~
@1000046 = ~Now then, you two have a long journey to take, and I have proper business to attend to. Out of my way.~
@1000047 = ~I hear your voice... you come into view. ~
@1000048 = ~I hear your voice... you come into view. ~
@1000049 = ~Gorion.~
